---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const props = {
	title: "shai",
	tagline:
		"Natural-language shell with typed slot filling. The model never touches your filesystem; you do.",
	description:
		"Type plain English; shai asks the model for a structured command spec, walks you through typed parameter slots, confirms once, then runs.",
	status: "in-progress" as const,
	startDate: "2026",
	type: "tooling" as const,
	role: "Solo",
	stack: ["Rust", "Anthropic API"],
	links: {
		repo: "https://github.com/gosamab/shai",
	},
	relatedProjects: [
		{ slug: "open-security", title: "Open Security" },
		{ slug: "content-creator", title: "Content Creator" },
	],
	toc: [
		{ id: "what-it-does", label: "What it does" },
		{ id: "why-slot-filling", label: "Why slot filling" },
		{ id: "the-keys", label: "Confirmation keys" },
	],
};
---

<ProjectLayout {...props}>
	<h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
	<p>
		Type a request in plain English. shai asks the model for a
		<em>structured</em> command, not a string, then walks you through
		filling typed parameter slots, confirms once, and runs it. The
		model never touches your filesystem; you do.
	</p>
	<pre><code class="text-sm">$ shai "find rust files modified in the last day"

Description:  Find files matching a name pattern, modified within a time window
🍵  find {`{path}`} -name '*.rs' -mtime -{`{days}`}

> Where to search: .
> Days: 1

🍵  find . -name '*.rs' -mtime -1
[Enter] run   [e] edit   [?] explain   [q] abort</code></pre>

	<h2 id="why-slot-filling">Why slot filling</h2>
	<p>
		shai asks the model for a <em>typed spec</em> (<code>path</code>,
		<code>number</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>path-must-exist</code>)
		and elicits each slot with the right widget instead of handing you
		a raw command string to edit free-form. Two safety wins:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Destructive commands get an extra gate.</strong> A typed
			<code>yes</code> is required for <code>rm</code>, <code>dd</code>,
			<code>kill</code>, etc., with no Enter shortcut.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Missing env vars are caught before execution.</strong> If
			the spec references <code>$AWS_PROFILE</code> and it isn't set,
			shai blocks the run.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="the-keys">Confirmation keys</h2>
	<p>After slot fill, shai shows the rendered command and a single-keystroke prompt.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><code>Enter</code> / <code>y</code>: run</li>
		<li><code>e</code>: open <code>$EDITOR</code> on the rendered command, then re-confirm</li>
		<li><code>?</code>: show description, warnings, reasoning; re-prompt</li>
		<li><code>q</code> / <code>n</code> / <code>Esc</code> / <code>Ctrl+C</code>: abort</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Beyond the basic flow, shai has <code>chat</code> (multi-turn REPL),
		<code>explain</code> (command → plain English), <code>install</code>
		(shell binding so <code>Alt+Enter</code> invokes shai on the current
		line), <code>history</code>, and pipe-friendly stdin mode (e.g.
		<code>git diff | shai "commit msg"</code>).
	</p>
</ProjectLayout>
